diff --git a/research/reader-w57-pilot/README.md b/research/reader-w57-pilot/README.md
index a4b5816..2dcad2c 100644
--- a/research/reader-w57-pilot/README.md
+++ b/research/reader-w57-pilot/README.md
@@ -86,3 +86,17 @@ W47 and W51 local screenshots (18 November 2026) show the original behavior:
 the panel control belonged to the right panel and appeared at the top when
 folded and in the panel header when open. W57 is the latest accepted styling
 reference; 'ARGON' is the design prototype name, not the website/Reader brand.
+
+### Mobile entry on the canonical reader
+
+`?reader-pilot=1` selects one layout on entry. Up through 1120 CSS px it keeps the
+native Reader and loads personal annotations only if the document has the
+canonical `#gbrMarginalia` tabpanel and its native controls. Wider entries keep
+the previous desktop pilot. A mobile route with no compatible tabpanel simply
+keeps the native Reader without adding an entry. Normal URLs remain unchanged.
+
+Layout selection is fixed for the document: rotating does not reparent native
+controls, recreate the overlay or discard a draft. When manually moving across
+the desktop/mobile breakpoint, reload to request the other layout. This avoids
+an automatic reload while a note is being edited; live migration of an already
+reparented desktop shell is not supported.
